# 3. LONG

In the morning, Esmeralda, the girl's mother, gave the basket of food to Maria, the girl in the red hood, who was carrying food to her sick grandmother. Esmeralda warned Maria, “Stay on the path.”

In the dark woods, Maria met Grumple, the hungry wolf. Grumple asked her, “Where are you going?” Maria answered, “To grandmother's cottage.” Grumple reached grandmother's cottage and swallowed Monique, the sick grandmother, who lived there alone. Grumple then disguised himself as Monique in the bed, waiting there in disguise.

In the afternoon at grandmother's cottage, Maria said, “What big eyes you have.” Gary, the passing woodcutter, intervened and cut Grumple open. Monique was alive and emerged.

